  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This tagine serves 4 and takes around 20 minutes to prepare and an hour on the hob. The long, slow braise is what transforms everyday chicken thighs into something deeply flavoured and falling-off-the-bone tender."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: Use only the rind of the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "preserved-lemon-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "preserved lemon"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and discard the pulp, which can turn bitter during cooking. Rinse the rind briefly under cold water to control the saltiness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
